# Line endings are NOT a style question here: a shell script checked out with CRLF fails at its
# first line, because `set -euo pipefail\r` makes bash reject `pipefail` as an invalid option name
# -- and the carriage return then mangles the error message itself, so it does not even read as a
# line-ending problem. Seen on a machine with core.autocrlf=true; the committed blobs were clean LF.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the WORKING TREE, so it holds regardless of the cloning machine's autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh       text eol=lf
*.sbatch   text eol=lf
*.py       text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
*.toml     text eol=lf
*.html     text eol=lf

*.npz  binary
*.png  binary
*.gif  binary
*.json binary
